@AppointmentService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5138

### Full health report, including the database check
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/health

### Liveness only — does not touch the database
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/health/live

### OpenAPI document
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json

### Swagger UI is served at {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/swagger
### Click "Authorize" there and paste the accessToken from one of the /auth/login calls below
### (no "Bearer " prefix needed) to call the protected endpoints from the browser.


### ===== Demo data (seeded automatically on first run, see AppointmentDbInitializer) =====
# DemoClinicId          11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
# DemoSecondClinicId    11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112
# DemoVeterinarianId       22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221  (Dr. Ana Petrova, General Practice, Central Vet Clinic) -- also "vet1"'s user id
# DemoSecondVeterinarianId 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222  (Dr. Marko Ivanov, Surgery, Central Vet Clinic)
# DemoThirdVeterinarianId  22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222223  (Dr. Elena Trajkova, Dermatology, North Animal Hospital)
# DemoOwnerId           33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333  (already has one upcoming appointment) -- also "owner1"'s user id
# DemoPetId             44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444


### ===== Auth (section 9) — everything below needs a token; see TestUsers =====
### owner1 / Owner123!       -> role "owner"        (user id = DemoOwnerId, see above)
### vet1   / Vet123!         -> role "veterinarian"  (user id = DemoVeterinarianId, see above)
### admin1 / Admin123!       -> role "admin"
### Outside Docker these hit the locally-signed fallback (TestUsers); in Docker /auth/login
### proxies these same credentials to the real Keycloak realm instead (see AuthController).

### Log in as the owner. Capture the token so the requests below can reuse it automatically.
POST {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "owner1",
  "password": "Owner123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("ownerToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### Log in as the admin (needed if you want to test admin-only paths — same booking/cancel/
### reschedule endpoints also accept "admin", not just "owner").
POST {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin1",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### Log in as the veterinarian — can view catalog/upcoming endpoints, but NOT book/cancel/
### reschedule (those require "owner" or "admin"); try this token against POST /appointments
### below to see the 403.
POST {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "vet1",
  "password": "Vet123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("vetToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### List all clinics
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/clinics
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### Search clinics by location
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/clinics?location=Skopje
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### List all veterinarians
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/veterinarians
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### Veterinarians at one clinic
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/veterinarians?clinicId=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### Veterinarians by specialization
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/veterinarians?specialization=Surgery
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### Open availability slots for a specific veterinarian (copy an AvailabilitySlotId from the
### response — you'll need one to book below)
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/slots?veterinarianId=22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### Open availability slots on a specific date
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/slots?date=2026-08-06
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### Upcoming appointments for the demo owner (should show the pre-seeded "Annual check-up")
GET {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/appointments/upcoming?ownerId=33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### Book an appointment — replace availabilitySlotId with one from the search above.
### NOTE: pet-ownership verification is faked (PetService:UseFakeVerification=true in
### appsettings.Development.json and in docker-compose.yml) since Pet Service doesn't have its
### /exists endpoint or any seeded pets/owners yet — any non-empty petId/ownerId is accepted.
### Any GUIDs work, but the demo ones above (DemoPetId/DemoOwnerId) are convenient since they also
### show up in "upcoming". Once Pet Service is ready, flip that flag off to hit the real service.
POST {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "petId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "ownerId": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333",
  "availabilitySlotId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "reason": "Routine vaccination"
}

### Same booking attempt, but as the veterinarian — should fail with 403 (only owner/admin can book).
POST {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{vetToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "petId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "ownerId": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333",
  "availabilitySlotId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "reason": "Routine vaccination"
}

### Same booking attempt again, but with no Authorization header at all — should fail with 401.
POST {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "petId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "ownerId": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333",
  "availabilitySlotId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "reason": "Routine vaccination"
}

### Cancel an appointment — replace {id} with an AppointmentId from a previous response.
### Reason is optional and passed as a query string (DELETE doesn't carry a conventional body).
DELETE {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/appointments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000?reason=Owner requested cancellation
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### Reschedule an appointment onto a different open slot — replace both ids.
PUT {{AppointmentService_HostAddress}}/appointments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newAvailabilitySlotId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}
